What is Robotic Drilling?
Robotic Drilling refers to the deployment of advanced automation technologies in drilling operations to enhance precision, safety, and efficiency. Robotic drilling systems utilize robotic manipulators, automated rig floor equipment, intelligent sensors, and AI-driven software platforms to manage critical processes such as pipe handling, torque application, real-time parameter adjustments, and wellbore navigation. These systems are applied across onshore, offshore, and directional drilling operations in the oil & gas industry, with growing relevance in mining and geothermal sectors.
